# Cloudflare static-assets headers.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security headers, site-wide.
#
# The audit found none were being sent. This is a static site with no cookies,
# no login and no user input, so the exposure is limited — but these are free
# and Google treats HTTPS/security hygiene as a quality signal.
#
# CSP allows no third-party origins at all — the site loads nothing external.
#
# script-src NEEDS 'unsafe-inline'. An earlier revision of this file set
# `script-src 'self'` and claimed it "stays clean"; that was wrong and it
# broke the live site — React never hydrated and the console filled with
# ~48 violations per page. Next's App Router inlines the RSC flight payload
# as `<script>self.__next_f.push(...)</script>` tags in every page, and they
# are not optional. The two ways out both fail here:
#
#   - Hashes: there are 1,162 unique inline scripts across the 140 exported
#     pages (the payload differs per page), which is ~64KB of sha256 hashes
#     in a single header. Far past any header size limit.
#   - Nonces: require generating a fresh value per response, i.e. a server.
#     `output: "export"` has none. A Worker could inject nonces with
#     HTMLRewriter, but that puts HTML rewriting in front of every request
#     on a service with a 1.8s LCP budget. Not worth it.
#
# What's recovered instead, since the site provably contains none of these
# (verified against out/**/*.html: 0 iframes, 0 inline event handlers,
# 0 javascript: URLs):
#
#   - script-src-attr 'none'  blocks onclick="..." style handlers, which
#     'unsafe-inline' in script-src would otherwise re-permit. This is the
#     bulk of what a real injection would try to use.
#   - frame-ancestors 'none' + X-Frame-Options DENY. Nothing frames this
#     site, and a clickjack overlay on a page whose whole purpose is a
#     tap-to-call button is a live risk, not a theoretical one.
#   - object-src 'none', base-uri 'self' unchanged.
#
# form-action stays 'self' rather than 'none' (there are currently no forms)
# so a Phase 7 booking form doesn't fail silently. If that form posts to a
# third party, its origin must be added here.
#
# Phase 7 analytics are Cloudflare Web Analytics, allow-listed above:
# static.cloudflareinsights.com (the beacon script) and cloudflareinsights.com
# (where it reports). Cookie-less, so no consent banner. The tap tracking
# beacon posts to /api/track on this origin and needs no extra permission.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; script-src-attr 'none'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The OG image is a metadata route emitting a real PNG at an extensionless
# path (/opengraph-image). Without an extension the asset server falls back to
# application/octet-stream, and WhatsApp/Facebook then refuse to render the
# share preview — which matters here because WhatsApp is a primary channel
# for this market. These rules pin the correct type.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Content-hashed build output is immutable by construction.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /admin — the staff dashboard. It is the ONLY place Firebase is allowed.
#
# The site-wide policy above stays strict: the public pages load nothing from
# a third party, which is what keeps them fast for someone in an emergency.
# This rule relaxes script-src/connect-src for the dashboard alone, and is
# more specific so it wins for these paths.
#
# noindex here as well as in the page's own meta and in robots.txt — three
# independent signals, because an indexed staff dashboard is not recoverable
# once it is in someone's search results.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/admin/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Cache-Control: no-store
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.firebaseio.com https://*.firebasedatabase.app https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com https://securetoken.googleapis.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'
